= Sequence annotation — Technical =

An annotation can be represented as a typed feature linked to a sequence interval or entity, with coordinates, strand/frame where relevant, ontology/vocabulary terms, evidence, source, confidence and version. Coordinate transforms and assembly/version changes can invalidate naive reuse, so provenance is essential.

== Modeling / evidence cautions ==
* annotation ≠ sequence
* predicted annotation ≠ experimentally validated function
* annotation version ≠ timeless fact

